CloudBurrow patch 65 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1584).

The bug: a CREATE TABLE (or CREATE VIEW, or a CREATE TABLE AS SELECT) in
a dataset that does not exist made the engine's table, committed it, and
only then failed, when syncCatalog's addTableMetadata found the dataset
missing ("dataset nods is not found"). The table stayed: the same
statement run again failed "failed to exec CREATE TABLE nods.x (a
INT64): sqlite3: SQL logic error: table `p_nods_x` already exists". And
through jobs.insert the error was answered with no job, where BigQuery
makes the job and fails it.

The patch looks for the datasets of the tables a query added before it
commits: each table whose dataset does not exist is dropped in the
query's transaction and taken out of the changed catalog. jobs.query
then fails with the same error as before ("dataset %s is not found",
which CloudBurrow's front answers 404 notFound), and jobs.insert records
the job, failed with it.

